# Question: when a config reload removes a container, is it sent its stop
# signal and then gone from the host, its control group, its root mount and
# the runtime library's state with it, while the daemon keeps running
# (spec-container-1-runtime AC-11, the container-stop-on-config-removal test)?
#
# A unit test cannot decide it: TestRemovedRootStopsEveryContainer proves the
# parser reads the change as "stop every container", and what this asks is
# whether a real reload reaches the plugin's worker and the real stop removes
# every trace on a real kernel.
#
# Method: the probe's drive mode starts the daemon itself, because a .ci line
# cannot change the config file between two observations. Once the container
# runs, drive overwrites the config with removed.conf, whose container root
# holds no instance, sends SIGHUP, and waits until the container has no
# control group, root mount or library state left and its stop signal is
# recorded. It then stops the daemon.
#
# The store lives under /run, not in the test's work directory: in the QEMU
# guest that directory is on the 9p share of the checkout, and an overlay
# cannot take a 9p directory as its upper layer.
option=needs-linux:caps=sys-admin
option=exclusive:group=container
option=timeout:value=150s
option=env:var=ze.test.container.store:value=/run/ze-container-test-$PORT

tmpfs=container.conf:terminator=EOF_CONFIG
container {
	instance probe {
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG

tmpfs=removed.conf:terminator=EOF_REMOVED
container {
}
EOF_REMOVED

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-containerprobe reset /run/ze-container-test-$PORT:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-containerprobe drive /run/ze-container-test-$PORT probe container.conf remove removed.conf:timeout=120s:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the container runs
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its control group is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its root mount is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its runtime library state is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the container received a stop signal
reject=stdout:contains=probe: FAIL
